  "notes": [
    "A missing charter update now always blocks as `[fix-required]`; no override can approve it away.",
    "A HIGH or CRITICAL dangerous pattern no longer blocks under the default policy: the commit passes with an \"Architect attention required\" warning and creates no override state.",
    "The external-approval envelope (#34, #35) is unchanged and now applies only where a mode requires it (Enterprise `evidence_only`), which also reports its outcome by category in `status.json` and the whiteboard.",
    "A block or approval left by an earlier Gator runtime is never reinterpreted: the commit blocks until it is cancelled and retried.",
    "When the Architect keeps a warning, the commit draft can record that decision; the hook checks it against the staged change, fails closed on stale or invented keys, and adds `Gator-Dangerous-Pattern-*` trailers that never contain the matched text.",
    "The Commits view shows an \"Architect acknowledgement\" note, kept apart from overrides by its label and glyph.",
    "Fleet and Settings show the commit policy as read-only text (Default, Legacy warn/off, or Managed by Enterprise) instead of the misleading strict/warn/off selector.",
    "A new Docs page, \"The Gator pre-commit checks\", explains the model to newcomers."
  ],
